  "surprise": "P46 SWA tail average (equal-weight mean of every post-step iterate from 75% of the 300 s budget, 1204/1121/1121 iterates at lr 0.40->0.30 of peak) on the 129-claude floor-0.3 incumbent scored 640/620/649 on seeds 0/1/2 versus 651/655/633: exact means 636.333333 versus 646.333333, -10.0; paired -11/-35/+16. Discard; inside the registered -30 to +30 range, below the +5 central guess. The pretraining side matched the prediction: the averaged weights had held-out greedy 0.985/0.983/0.986 (129: 0.963/0.964/0.955, back to 115's floor-0.1 level) and val_loss_avg 0.0830/0.0818/0.0815 versus the raw iterates' last-five-point mean 0.0843/0.0855/0.0809. RL started much stronger, round-1 solved 765/725/770 (129 seed 0: 647; 115 seed 0: 718), but RL-solved totals ended level, 1139/1101/1137 versus 1131/1122/1123 (means 1126 vs 1125), and eval at >=7 fell on two seeds. So the average acts like an annealed endpoint: it buys short-proof accuracy and a better first harvest, which the fixed RL catches up on anyway, and none of it carries to length >=7. With 048 (-12, five low-LR snapshots) this is the second weight-averaging handoff below its incumbent; better pretraining accuracy and loss are again not the lever for the downstream metric. Pretrain 300 s on every seed (averaging overhead negligible), totals 1501/1543/~1650 s, no timeout.",
